<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: TABLE - Bank of Ireland yr profit up 8.8 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Bank of Ireland yr profit up 8.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>(million punts unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		   52.0		vs 41.5</p>
<p> Dividend  (pence)	   11.65	     vs n/a</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence)    17.75	     vs 15.25</p>
<p> Pretax profit pre-exceps  395.6	     vs 363.7</p>
<p> Pretax profit post exceps 395.6	     vs 315.6</p>
<p> Loan loss provisions	20.0		vs 21.4</p>
<p> Total income		  923.3	     vs 856.3</p>
<p> Net interest income	 608.1	     vs 575.7</p>
<p> Total assets		  19,669.6	  vs 20,958.8</p>
<p> Capital ratios (pct)	16.3		vs 14.0</p>
<p> Tier 1 capital ratio (pct)11.0		vs 9.5</p>
<p> Operating expenses	  543.0	     vs 520.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the Irish commercial bank and financial group is Bank of Ireland Plc. Analysts had forecast pretax profits around 400 million Irish pounds and a total dividend of 17.5/18.0p per share. The bank said it was optimistic for the future. &quot;In the circumstances, a positive view of the group's future performance is justified,&quot; the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>--Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
